# Client — Angular App

## Layout

```text
app.ts / app.config.ts / app.routes.ts   → app entry (avoid parallel edits)
core/      → guards, interceptors, services, models
features/  → lazy-loaded areas (auth, recipes, cooking, ai-import, categories)
shared/    → reusable components, pipes, directives
```

## Conventions

- **Standalone components only** — no NgModules. App-wide providers in `app.config.ts`.
- **Lazy load** every feature via `loadChildren` in `app.routes.ts`.
- **i18n:** route all user-facing strings through ngx-translate — no hardcoded text.
- **RTL/LTR:** use logical CSS (`margin-inline`, `padding-inline`, `text-align: start/end`).
- **Prettier:** `printWidth: 100`, `singleQuote: true`.

## Example — logical CSS for RTL

```scss
// ✅ GOOD
.card {
  margin-inline-start: 1rem;
  text-align: start;
}

// ❌ BAD — breaks in RTL
.card {
  margin-left: 1rem;
  text-align: left;
}
```

## Commands

```bash
cd client && npm start        # http://localhost:4200
cd client && npm run build && npm test
```

Run build and tests before proposing a merge.
